	(text "Thermal pad: solder to GND plane, thermal vias"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.86 82.55 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9705f8d0-056f-4e92-9bf8-3dc5a4445058")
	)
	(text "CURRENT AND THERMAL LIMITS\n- ITRIP regulation: 6.5 A at power-up (ITRIP_LVL = 4 / 5.4 / 6.5 / 7 A). The driver chops\n  on its own above this level. Set DIS_ITRIP = 11b if only the INA240 loop should act\n- OCP: 10 A min, latched shutdown by default (OCP_MODE)\n- Rds(on) HS + LS = 150 mOhm typ at 25 C (rises when hot). P = I^2 x 0.15 Ohm:\n  1.4 W at 3 A, 2.4 W at 4 A, 3.8 W at 5 A. RthJA about 28 C/W on 4 layers\n  -> plan for about 3.5 A continuous per axis without extra cooling; TSD at 165 C\n- No output filter: OUT1 / OUT2 go straight to the coil. Edge rate is set by SR (SPI),\n  10.8 V/us at power-up: slow it down there if the coil leads radiate too much\n- LAYOUT: C309 at VM pin 20, C310 at VM pin 13, C304 / C312 at pins 21-23, C305 at pin 1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 152.4 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9958bd4b-4b7b-47e9-9a33-49ca431d4960")
	)
	(text "DISABLE = 0: bridge on"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 114.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9a50575c-0ae9-443b-a02d-cc631eb25f10")
	)
	(text "VM snubber"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.49 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f15d0a6d-649e-4eeb-b980-5d4405e906f4")
	)
	(text "DRV8873S NOTES (per axis)\n- Supply: VM = +24 V only (4.5-38 V). Charge pump (C304, C312) and 5 V DVDD regulator (C305) are internal,\n  so the 12 V gate supply, bootstrap caps and OC_ADJ resistor of the DRV8412 are gone\n- PWM_A -> PH/IN2 -> OUT2 = OUT_A (coil +, through the shunt). PWM_B -> EN/IN1 -> OUT1 = OUT_B (coil -).\n  Crossed on purpose: OUT2 / OUT1 then face the + / - coil connectors without crossing on the PCB\n- Power-up default, no SPI needed: PWM mode (MODE = 01b). One input high = drive, both high = brake\n  (high-side recirculation), both low = Hi-Z (coast)\n- Recommended: write MODE = 10b (independent half bridge) over SPI. Each OUTx then follows its INx like\n  the DRV8412 did, so PWM_A = D, PWM_B = 1-D, unipolar, 20 kHz works unchanged\n- DISABLE tied to GND: the bridge is on whenever the driver is awake\n- ~{SLEEP}: 10k pull-down. Set high, wait >= 1.5 ms (tWAKE), then configure over SPI. Its high level\n  also sets the SDO logic level (3.3 V from the STM32)\n- ~{FAULT}: open drain, 10k pull-up to 3.3 V. Low on UVLO, charge-pump UV, OCP, TSD, open load\n  (also low briefly during wake-up). No OTW pin: over-temperature warning is the OTW bit in the\n  FAULT register (or on nFAULT if OTW_REP = 1)\n- SPI: mode 1 (CPOL = 0, CPHA = 1), 16-bit frames, MSB first. SCLK / SDI / SDO are shared by X, Y, Z;\n  one ~{SCS} per axis (SDO is Hi-Z while ~{SCS} is high)\n- Clear a latched fault: CLR_FLT bit over SPI (preferred) or a 5-20 us low pulse on ~{SLEEP}"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ffd2da35-bbb3-4ff4-bbc8-06a71600c6f9")
	)
